# Merge reusable source meshes into one indexed, colored draw without host geometry code.
import scene_mesh.dl
import scene_transforms.dl

UI mesh vertex list means: the type of (an empty list of UI mesh vertex)
UI mesh index list means: the type of (an empty list of a 32 bit unsigned integer)
UI mesh color list means: the type of (an empty list of linear UI paint)

class:
    patterns:
        UI mesh builder
    members:
        vertices as UI mesh vertex list
        indices as UI mesh index list
        colors as UI mesh color list

to get [a UI mesh builder]:
    return storage for one slot initialized with @intrinsic("construct", UI mesh builder, an empty list of UI mesh vertex, an empty list of a 32 bit unsigned integer, an empty list of linear UI paint)

to [append UI mesh] {UI scene mesh:mesh} [through] {UI scene transform:transform} [tinted] {linear UI paint:tint} [to] {a pointer to UI mesh builder:builder}:
    set base to the length of (builder's vertices)
    set index to 0
    for each vertex in mesh's vertices:
        set point to the UI scene position of (the UI mesh position of vertex) through transform
        set normal to (the UI scene normal vector of (the UI mesh normal of vertex) through transform) normalized
        append UI mesh vertex at point normal normal uv (vertex's u as a floating-point number) (vertex's v as a floating-point number) to (builder's vertices)
        set source to the item at index in mesh's colors
        append (linear UI ink red (source's red * tint's red) green (source's green * tint's green) blue (source's blue * tint's blue)) to (builder's colors)
        increment index
    set index to 0
    loop while index < the length of mesh's indices:
        set first to (the item at index in mesh's indices) as an integer
        set second to (the item at (index + 1) in mesh's indices) as an integer
        set third to (the item at (index + 2) in mesh's indices) as an integer
        if transform's handedness > 0.0:
            append UI mesh triangle (base + first) (base + second) (base + third) to (builder's indices)
        else:
            append UI mesh triangle (base + first) (base + third) (base + second) to (builder's indices)
        set index to index + 3

to [close UI mesh builder] {a pointer to UI mesh builder:builder}:
    free builder's vertices
    free builder's indices
    free builder's colors
    destroy the value at builder
    deallocate builder

to get [a completed UI mesh from] {a pointer to UI mesh builder:builder}:
    set result to a UI scene mesh taking vertices (builder's vertices) and indices (builder's indices) and colors (builder's colors)
    close UI mesh builder builder
    return result
